      {
        "id": 46530,
        "name": "James 'Buster' Douglas Knock Out Boxing",
        "summary": "Final Blow is an action game based around the sport of boxing. You can play the fighters in a sequence of knock-out competitions, (the computer versions also include a round-robin league). Rounds last one minute, with a short break in between them. As in the real sport, your aim is to knock your opponent down for 10 seconds, by gradually weakening him with a series of punches. You can block punches, to avoid them inflicting damage onto you. The ring is of a limited size, so players can be cornered, although the referee will intervene to break the boxers up if they become entangled in a stalemate position.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/sq4oozb4fiqqdcxtd5az.jpg",
